    and Ludwig Göransson won in consecutive years (though Desplat's wins were non-consecutive). The 2020s, still 
    incomplete, have already reversed this trend dramatically — with Ludwig Göransson winning three times in four 
    years (2023, 2024, 2026) and Hans Zimmer returning after a 27-year gap.
  </p>
  <div class="insight">
    <strong>Insight:</strong> The first-time winner rate has fluctuated between 50% and 100% by decade. 
    The 1950s (50%) and 1990s (60%) were eras of established-composer dominance, while the 1930s (100%), 
    2010s (90%), and 1960s–1970s (80%) favored new voices.
  </div>
  <h3>Back-to-Back Wins: A Rare Feat</h3>
