    <strong>Franz Waxman</strong> achieved it first (1950–1951) with two dramatically different films: 
    <em>Sunset Boulevard</em> and <em>A Place in the Sun</em>. <strong>Alan Menken</strong> followed four decades 
    later (1991–1992) during Disney's animation dominance. <strong>Gustavo Santaolalla</strong> repeated the feat 
    (2005–2006) with <em>Brokeback Mountain</em> and <em>Babel</em>, and <strong>Ludwig Göransson</strong> 
    became the most recent back-to-back winner (2023–2024) for <em>Oppenheimer</em>.
  </p>
