    while <strong>Alfred Newman</strong>, <strong>Miklos Rozsa</strong>, and <strong>Franz Waxman</strong> built the 
    orchestral vocabulary that would dominate cinema for decades. With 25 unique composers across 26 ceremonies, 
    this era was relatively open — the studio system employed a deep roster of talent, and no single voice could 
    monopolize the award.
  </p>

  <h3><span class="era-badge era-silver">Silver Age · 1960–1979</span></h3>
  <p>
